@startuml
!include ../_style.iuml
title Epic 6 — Settings, observability and prompt versions

rectangle "Settings" {
  card US6_1 [
    **US-6.1  Choose the models per notebook**
    As a //reader//, I want to pick the chat and embedding model for each notebook
    (local Ollama, NVIDIA, OpenRouter, OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Cohere),
    so that I can trade quality, cost and privacy.
    ----
    * Changing the embedding model rebuilds that notebook's index.
    * Temperature, answer length, chunk size and overlap are per notebook.
  ]
}
rectangle "Operations" {
  card US6_2 [
    **US-6.2  See what the model saw**
    As an //operator//, I want one trace per answer with every step and model call nested in it,
    so that I can debug a bad answer from the prompt that produced it.
    ----
    * Langfuse shows guardrails, plan, retrieval, rerank, sub-answers, synthesis and tokens.
    * Worker tasks continue the trace of the request that queued them.
  ]
  card US6_3 [
    **US-6.3  Change a prompt without a deploy**
    As an //operator//, I want prompts versioned in Langfuse and served by label,
    so that I can roll a prompt forward or back from the UI.
    ----
    * The locale files are the source of truth and the fallback.
    * A version with a broken placeholder falls back to the local text.
  ]
  card US6_4 [
    **US-6.4  Watch the system's health**
    As an //operator//, I want Prometheus metrics and Grafana dashboards,
    so that I can see latency, errors, queue depth and model time at a glance.
  ]
  card US6_5 [
    **US-6.5  See under the hood without leaving the app**
    As a //signed-in user//, I want dashboards, traces, tasks and queues inside the app,
    so that I can show what the system is doing without juggling four other tabs.
    ----
    * One Visualization button opens Grafana, Langfuse, Flower and RabbitMQ in frames.
    * Traces open on the notebook that is on screen.
    * Grafana, Flower and RabbitMQ are served only to a signed-in user.
    * A tool that is not running says so; the button is hidden when none is configured.
  ]
}
US6_1 -[hidden]down- US6_2
US6_2 -[hidden]down- US6_3
US6_3 -[hidden]down- US6_4
US6_4 -[hidden]down- US6_5
@enduml
